  "description": "Plakar keeps default FastCDC (about 1 MiB), LZ4 stream compression and backup-cache policy. Repository creation disables encryption with -plaintext; the adapter uses -stdio, -quiet and -no-progress. Recovery restores over existing output; repository check is separate. Gutch uses unencrypted FastCDC with a 1 MiB target, LZ4 0 and 8 MiB bundles. Chunk bounds, LZ4 implementation/framing, metadata and storage layout differ; stored Plakar level 9 is not passed to its stream writer. Fresh local repositories and isolated caches; automatic workers; noninteractive/output flags. One warm-up and 3 rotating measured repetitions, profiling off. Independent validation is outside timings; extra files are allowed.",
